# PATCH: 005-disable-printing
#
# DenBrowser removes printing from production builds with Firefox 153's real
# --disable-printing configure option. PrintingEnabled=false policy and the
# locked print.enabled=false preference retain the supported runtime gates.
#
# gfx/thebes/moz.build also omits the platform PrintTargetPDF, PrintTargetCG,
# and PrintTargetWindows implementations when NS_PRINTING is false. Android and
# Cocoa print sources, factories, and component registrations now follow the
# same gate, keeping their consumers aligned with Cairo and the graphics targets.
#
# This patch also keeps source-level enforcement for direct callers and custom
# printing-enabled builds:
#
# - Browser commands remain dispatchable under the locked preference so Ctrl+P
#   and command-bound UI can report the block. Browser commands, hardware print
#   commands, frame/selection context actions, BrowserDOMWindow OPEN_PRINT_BROWSER
#   routes, the Save as PDF quick action, and direct print-dialog opens notify and
#   return before tab-dialog modal state, progress listeners, preview browsers,
#   print services, or IPC are initialized.
#
# - WebExtension tabs.print and tabs.saveAsPDF return before PrintUtils, a file
#   picker, output stream, or print promise is created. saveAsPDF resolves with
#   "not_saved".
#
# - PrintUtils and print.js stop page setup, preview, silent/system printing,
#   and direct-dialog initialization before cloning or opening native UI. The
#   direct print.html backstop also avoids acquiring nsIPrintSettingsService at
#   module evaluation.
#
# - nsGlobalWindowOuter blocks window.print() and internal content callers;
#   CanonicalBrowsingContext rejects parent print promises before analysis,
#   cloning, RemotePrintJob creation, or PBrowser IPC; nsPrintJob::CommonPrint
#   remains the final printing-enabled source backstop and follows existing
#   failure cleanup.
#
# DenBrowserPrintingChild/Parent are dedicated all-frame actors so subframe and
# popup attempts preserve their owning-tab/opener context. Firefox's stock
# Printing actor remains top-level-only. Patch 004 displays all feedback through
# the shared four-second, non-modal notification bar.


